in{aligned}(x-4)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta-4)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2} & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta+16+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta & =16 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-8r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ r(r-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\,4\\le z\\le 7\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}x^{2} + y^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186537027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e702de4-81fb-57f8-b700-52c7a2d5b037" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}^{-1}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186537029} {:answer/id #uuid "6eef909b-2ae7-54ad-8347-4b8012df300a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-1}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r